  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing life-saving services to injured in Gaza</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The idea of the project is to strengthen the capacities of Al-Awda Health &amp; Community Association to provide life-saving health services to the injured through its 8 health facilities due to the recent Israeli attacks on the Gaza Strip, which have claimed the lives of 31 martyrs so far, including 6 children &amp; 4 women, in addition to injuring 275 persons, as these services will contribute to saving the lives of the injured, reducing complications &amp; limiting disabilities, mainly children &amp; women.</narrative>
  </description>
